  "body": "### Summary\nAs a user of a strong gallery theme, I want every destructive button that sits in a themed list row to stay legible, so that « Repartir de zéro… » and the account sync reset read as clearly as the rest of the list. They keep the system red (3.75:1 on Noël abusé's `surface`).\n\n### Scope\nFound by the round-2 review of PR #1350 (#1121 covers only `AccountDeletionView` and `AccountsView`):\n- `UnreadableDataRecoveryButton` (`App/SwiftHFR/Common/UnreadableDataRecovery.swift`), used in `AccountDeletionView:126`, `SmileyPickerView:209`, `ImageUploadView:116`, `MPStorageSettingsSection:53`, `PseudoListEditorView:38`, `TopicListView:80`: it is shared, so check each call site is a themed list row before applying `themedDestructive()` inside it.\n- The account sync reset button, `SecuritySettingsSections.swift:33`.\n- Not alerts, dialogs, swipe actions, toolbars or `.plain` buttons.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `themedDestructive()` (#1121) applied where the button is a themed list row, with a rendered test per distinct placement.\n- [ ] Legacy pixel-identical.\n- [ ] THEMES.md §3 sentence updated (it names this follow-up).\n- [ ] Device check listed on #893.",
